  "description": "A simple, quick, and easy soup, this classic oyster stew is flecked with droplets of golden butter and flavored with aromatic vegetables, whole milk, and plenty of briny, fat oysters.",
  "notes": "Optional or for serving: Minced parsley, chives, tarragon, and/or fennel fronds, for garnish\n\nOptional substitutions: fresh thyme → 1 dried bay leaf\n\nNotes: If you don't have fennel, you can substitute 3 tablespoons of Pernod, added just before the milk.\nIf you don't want to shuck your own oysters, feel free to use pre-shucked fresh ones (along with their liquor) from your fishmonger.",
